","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T13:25:16-07:00","id":1213166,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember Demon the Descent having lizard people. Or am i remembering wrong?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T15:37:43-07:00","id":1213204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212368-fansplats?p=1213166#post1213166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to remember Demon the Descent having lizard people. Or am i remembering wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reptilians. Lizard Cryptids that can imitate people. Also lovably cowardly.<br /> <hr /><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23573\" data-vbnamecard=\"23573\">ThriceHonored</a> do you have any powers gimmicks in mind? Like Vampire's (2E) Disciplines have a base power that (mostly) others build off of, Werewolf's (2E) Gifts have different effects for each Facet of Renown, Mage's Arcana grant broad degree of effect options, etc.<br /> <br /> Ideas:<ul><li>Leverage &quot;Combos&quot; as a concept, such that certain powers require or have added effect if some other power (or Condition/Tilt?) is on the target.<ul><li>Good for martial arts feel.</li> <li>Could reference things like &quot;venoms&quot; or &quot;Constricted&quot; for the initial Conditions/Tilts</li> </ul></li> <li>Keep to area-wide effects (like Environmental Tilts, or Conditions that apply to everyone in an area).<ul><li>Maybe this is only one category of power (like Mummy has Affinities and Utterances).</li> </ul></li> <li>Have an entire powerset available, but mutually exclusive with other powersets. Characters can take time in between Chapters/Scenes to swap them out.<ul><li>This draws upon themes of a snake shedding its skin. The &quot;skin&quot; here being the powerset.</li> </ul></li> <li>Something from <a href=\"https://www.thoughtco.com/serpent-magic-and-symbolism-2562474\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>?</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-29-2018, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-29T20:44:55-07:00","id":1213307,"title":"","content":"Naga will be a game of glories now forgotten by the children (mortals) and kept secret by the keepers(naga.)<br /> The basis of this wisdom is essentially hermeticism. For millennia they disseminated wisdom to the deserving and took on a role as educators to the young mammals, but then they were betrayed. <br /> The priests of the merciless One God came and they were labeled heretics and demons. Today even self professed atheists often recoil from serpents. The distrust is ingrained deep now. <br /> Now knowledge is procured and kept for the benefit of the Keepers, because it is simply what they do. They have kept extensive oral and written histories in secret libraries all around the world. Histories of a world much older than the children believe possible. <br /> <br /> Serpents have been associated with life, death, wisdom, water, healing, and maybe a few other aspects I\u2019m forgetting. I\u2019m debating creating a magic system all their own devoted to these aspects. They won\u2019t do all a mage can do, nor should they, <br /> <br /> That being said primarily physical or social snakes will exist and shine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23573,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","user":"ThriceHonored","date":". 04-30-2018, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T06:25:54-07:00","id":1213400,"title":"","content":"With the inhuman teachers of ancient pre-human wisdom angle, you\u2019ll need to watch out for the bane of fansplats; overlapping thematic space with existing official splats. In this case, Beast (lessons) and Mummy (forgotten glories). <br /> <br /> (Not trying to shoot down the idea here, of course)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T11:49:25-07:00","id":1213495,"title":"","content":"The way I see them they used to teach humanity but after they fell out of favor they hoard it for themselves. That being said I would like to find a way for them to somehow stand opposed to the begotten because quite frankly I hate beast the primordial. <br /> <br /> When they were mentoring humanity I see them as actually teaching as opposed to beasts who just said they were but we\u2019re really just the glutting themselves on Being sociopaths","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23573,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","user":"ThriceHonored","date":". 04-30-2018, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T12:32:36-07:00","id":1213503,"title":"","content":"I have an image in my head of old secret libraries stacked with scrolls and hand written books and fragments. I don\u2019t think it would be wise to have them actually know everything though. History is longer than people expect and a lot of knowledge could be lost and have to be Rediscovered. The search could take you all over the world to secret libraries, forgotten depths, even to other realms such as the great library in the underworld or the hedge or the twilight","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T14:00:33-07:00","id":1213525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212368-fansplats?p=1213503#post1213503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an image in my head of old secret libraries stacked with scrolls and hand written books and fragments. I don\u2019t think it would be wise to have them actually know everything though. History is longer than people expect and a lot of knowledge could be lost and have to be Rediscovered. The search could take you all over the world to secret libraries, forgotten depths, even to other realms such as the great library in the underworld or the hedge or the twilight</div> </div> </div> </div>The Underworld containing a twisted, half-fake copy of all the information in the Library of Alexandria, or maybe just the stuff that can never be recovered by mortal means appeals to me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-30-2018, 07:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T15:43:15-07:00","id":1213550,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What about in addition to &quot;lore&quot; they also seek &quot;balance&quot;? Between the leaderless, homeless hunters (Werewolves), rampant symbols of oppression (Exarchs), vain feudings of Beast and Hero, parasitic drains upon the life of the world (Vampires and Mummies feeding Sekhem to the Judges), and a systematic <i>thing</i> that exploits this all for fuel (the God-Machine) - crap is seriously out of wack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T16:54:18-07:00","id":1213587,"title":"","content":"I think its' better to focus on how they work in a vacuum. Devote more word count to how their society works, how they interact with each other and vanilla humans. Then mention ways that they could interact with the other supernaturals. By all means, try to work out a lore that doesn't conflict egregiously with any other splats, but that seems like a secondary concern to me.<br /> <br /> Also, complaint I've seen a lot on both fan and official splats is that they sometimes forget that their protagonists are monsters. Not just weird creatures, but monsters with goals that humanity might not always agree with and the sort of power that corrupts absolutely. Never let the readers forget that for long.<br /> <br /> Also, had an idea based on your idea about half-snakes, W:tF's Firstborn and your Aboleth idea. What if there are only a handful of pureblooded naga left, but each of them is immensely powerful and is the progenitor of a lineage/esoteric tradition of half-blood Naga (your PCs) who compete for their ancestor's favor. Like Changeling, there would be five standard lineages, but room in the lore for more if STs think them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:49:30-07:00","id":1213630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212368-fansplats?p=1213587#post1213587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its' better to focus on how they work in a vacuum. Devote more word count to how their society works, how they interact with each other and vanilla humans. Then mention ways that they could interact with the other supernaturals. By all means, try to work out a lore that doesn't conflict egregiously with any other splats, but that seems like a secondary concern to me.<br /> <br /> Also, complaint I've seen a lot on both fan and official splats is that they sometimes forget that their protagonists are monsters. Not just weird creatures, but monsters with goals that humanity might not always agree with and the sort of power that corrupts absolutely. Never let the readers forget that for long.<br /> <br /> Also, had an idea based on your idea about half-snakes, W:tF's Firstborn and your Aboleth idea. What if there are only a handful of pureblooded naga left, but each of them is immensely powerful and is the progenitor of a lineage/esoteric tradition of half-blood Naga (your PCs) who compete for their ancestor's favor. Like Changeling, there would be five standard lineages, but room in the lore for more if STs think them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I was merely pointing out how the standard setting is full of things that could be considered &quot;out of balance&quot;. No need to refer to any of them, really. Especially when creating new antagonists. I just thought it might be a good <i>active</i> motivation to go with collecting lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-30T18:58:28-07:00","id":1213631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212368-fansplats?p=1213630#post1213630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I was merely pointing out how the standard setting is full of things that could be considered &quot;out of balance&quot;. No need to refer to any of them, really. Especially when creating new antagonists. I just thought it might be a good <i>active</i> motivation to go with collecting lore.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. You could even refer to real-world issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T04:30:27-07:00","id":1213737,"title":"","content":"Hm. I like the idea on lineages. One could be the Norse world serpent, another could be one of the serpent headed Egyptian gods, then one of the feathered serpents of South America...I\u2019ll do research into more mythological serpents...<br /> <br /> Hell one of them could be the serpent from he garden. The lost serpent, the one that started it all. Shrouded in legend and metaphor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:22:15-07:00","id":1213746,"title":"","content":"Aboriginal Australian's Rainbow <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainbow_Serpent\" target=\"_blank\">Serpent</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:34:04-07:00","id":1213748,"title":"","content":"Part I'd like to emphasize is that <i>they compete with each other</i>. I don't know much about vampire, but in the games I know, people in the same subsplat tend to at least tolerate and understand each other's perspectives. In this idea, the lineages, being partly non-social animals, compete within themselves more often than they compete with other lineages, as each lineage is searching for a different kind of lore. In fact, this might even assist in making mixed parties, as naga from different lineages could agree to pacts of mutual assistance and not get in the way of each other's research","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T05:57:21-07:00","id":1213765,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Serpent Must Teach&quot;<br /> <br /> If I may, it's not the seeking of knowledge that would be important to them, it's the <i>transference</i> of it. Often recklessly, given the world we're talking about.<br /> <br /> In the CofD, even <i>knowing </i>certain things can be super-dangerous, both to sanity, safety and your own soul. The Serpents don't... really account for that. They're not about wisdom--that's up to the pupil to achieve, but they'll lay out the building blocks they know, and what they know can often be literally transferred through their half-spirit blood.<br /> <br /> They'll teach what they can, to whom they can, driven to form clusters of students in a twisting nest--who themselves spread out and mature into civilization. Civilization that weaves into the cracks until it's own bulk pulls it down, or it finds something hostile in the Dark.<br /> <br /> My picture is of a parallel splat alongside the werewolves and the like, based on the logic of &quot;wolves only tell the stories that make them look good.&quot; That does <u>not</u> mean &quot;fansplat that can stand in werewolf's space&quot;, but something that could be used to tell an interesting story.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T06:50:36-07:00","id":1214137,"title":"","content":"I've been a big fan of using serpent people in games for a while. Reptilian people from underground being one of my go to tropes.<br /> <br /> I'm curious as to how you'll be fitting yours into the CoD. I usually do them as a lost civilization that got wiped out about the same time as the Dinosaurs with scattered colonies of varying degrees of civility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1776-sidious","name":"Sidious","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T11:10:56-07:00","id":1214224,"title":"","content":"I may also do my Aboleth splat too. My babies finally started taking naps so I\u2019m just looking to...well in the south we call it \u201cpiddling around.\u201d Something to keep my brain going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T13:26:40-07:00","id":1214294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThriceHonored</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1212368-fansplats?p=1214224#post1214224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may also do my Aboleth splat too. My babies finally started taking naps so I\u2019m just looking to...well in the south we call it \u201cpiddling around.\u201d Something to keep my brain going.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish mine still took naps reliably...<br /> <br /> What about &quot;combining&quot; it with the Naga/Serpents? Make one the Antagonist group of the other. You can share mythological elements and mechanical features, and eliminate the &quot;who are players playing against&quot; question <i>while</i> building in inherent &quot;greyness&quot; to the opposition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:56:47-07:00","id":1214537,"title":"","content":"I had thought about it, but I feel like the two pieces just don\u2019t lineup like I would want them to. With the serpents they have already been established in the world, been around thousands of years and either know or think they know quite a bit. With the aberrants I had thought about it, but I feel like the two pieces just don\u2019t lineup like I would want to. With the serpents they have already been established in the world, been around thousands of years and either know or think they know quite a bit. With the aberrant They have not been around for very long at all, the \u201csurfacing \u201c Only begin occurring around 100 years ago. They also do not have a lot of societal structure yet so the humans turned monsters are still figuring out the supernatural world it hides behind the \u201creal world\u201d. Only begin occurring around 100 years ago. They also do not have a lot of societal structure yet so the humans turned monsters are still figuring out the supernatural world it hides behind the \u201creal world\u201c. In the serpents case I see them running the gamut from Saintly Two sociopathy. The aberrant lose their concept of good and evil. They run the spectrum from seeing the world like Spock to like a small child new to the world.Of course just when you begin to judge them by a human meter stick they may do something completely alien and in human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T04:57:21-07:00","id":1214538,"title":"","content":"Also if anyone ever sees a glaring typos or grammar problem it is because I am using talk to text while trying to wash and or change a baby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T04:10:03-07:00","id":1214984,"title":"","content":"You know you could combine the two in another Way. The Serpents have a consistent enemy the &quot;Rises&quot; Regularly and seeks to pervert all the Teachings of the Serpents... That would be the Aberrants. To do it right... Perhaps the Serpents and the Aberrant were once.. the Same Race. The Serpents recorded Knowledge and passed it down and a sub-sect of them developed a &quot;New Method&quot; of storing it and passing it along. Genetically. They developed a method that would allow the Knowledge to be stored inside of themselves, it worked, but.. went wrong.<br /> <br /> In some of the Serpents it would transform them into a strange creature that doesn't care. At All, It still wants to spread the Knowledge, but.. that knowledge is Warped and twisted. Dangerous to know, altering people's minds and eventually their bodies into fellow Aberrations. The Serpents oppose them because they are a direct threat to what they are trying to do themselves.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Reason the Serpents retracted from the world in the first place is because of them in the first place. And when they rise (they'd probably be circular in this idea, Rising when they when they have regained strength or been woken) The Serpents come out too stop them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T21:57:06-07:00","id":1215355,"title":"","content":"Alright. Going into hermit mode to work think and talk to an infant more than I do to adults.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T03:15:06-07:00","id":1217920,"title":"","content":"3 forms. Human, Snake, Naga. Human is self explanatory. Snake form is either a real world species or a close analogue, player could choose between a stealthy,strong, or poisonous variety. Naga is a reptilian humanoid torso on a long snake body. Going monstrous with no legs but reigning it in by keeping a flat more human (if scaley) face, <br /> <br /> Working on progenitors now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T05:19:28-07:00","id":1217932,"title":"","content":"The snake form could be informed by the X or Z splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T01:14:10-07:00","id":1218437,"title":"","content":"Naga The Forgotten <br /> <br /> Powerstat: chakra 1-7 awarded in game achievement not bought with experience. Each level has a benefit.<br /> Fuel Stat: akasha <br /> Morality: kundalini <br /> <br /> Three forms: human guise<br /> Naga<br /> Serpent<br /> <br /> Naga innate abilities:<br /> -can see heat when needed<br /> -enhanced scent via tongue<br /> <br /> Minor abilities- orisons <br /> Major abilities-meditations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23573-thricehonored","name":"ThriceHonored","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}